The shop assistant returns with the new t-shirt.
"Here is size L," she says.
"Thank you very much," I answer.
This time I go straight to the fitting room.
I go into a cubicle and try on the yellow t-shirt.
I look in the mirror and am very relieved.
It fits perfectly.
The t-shirt is no longer too small.
It is much more comfortable at the shoulders than the first t-shirt.
I get dressed again.
